<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Herzberg am Harz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Herzberg am <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harz">Harz</a> is a town on the south-western edge of the Harz in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Its hilltop castle served as a residence of the Guelph dukes of Grubenhagen until their line died out in 1596, after which it passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneburg">Lüneburg</a> and Hanoverian branches. The half-timbered castle is one of the largest of its kind in Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herzberg-am-harz.jpg" alt="Herzberg am Harz" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Binder · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Herzberg_Schlossblick.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
